From 16f638efbddaa88ea035771762e44eacd097921f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:16:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gcode): the Klartext reader reads tapping cycles
 206/207, the cycle 9 dwell and cycle 32

Second slice of the HEIDENHAIN Klartext reader. It now reads back every
block that the Klartext post writes today:

- CYCL DEF 206 (floating tap holder) and CYCL DEF 207 (rigid tapping,
  feed S x Q239 at the call; a left-hand thread is refused by name).
- CYCL DEF 9.0 / 9.1 DWELL, recorded as a dwell event.
- CYCL DEF 32.0 / 32.1 / 32.2 TOLERANCE, checked, no path change.
- Sub-block order is enforced; other sub-block cycles stay refused.
- cl::Cycle entry_z is the surface Q203 for Klartext hole cycles.

The round trip covers picomax_cycles.nc against cycles.cnc, and every
.nc golden of the Klartext post must parse. Truncation and seeded
mutation tests cover the cycle golden too.

Refs #2227

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
